From edf11ddd623bf71e8d044148025eab45b949ef8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:29:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: t8152-aop-audio: serve speaker sense from a
 driver-owned ring

On T8142 and T6050 multi-amp speaker streams, the AOP firmware's
serializer carries 8 or 12 16-bit V/I sense slots back on base-ns ADMAC
RX with no hardware frame-start marker. Previously, the sense front-end
opened the ADMAC channel directly and realigned it only when speaker
playback prepared a stopped serializer. When PipeWire stops, prepares
and restarts the sense front-end while the speaker serializer is already
running in pwrd (which happens deterministically on stream start and on
any capture XRUN recovery), the ADMAC RX channel restarts mid-frame at an
arbitrary 16-bit word offset modulo the channel count, misattributing V/I
sense samples across amplifiers.

Move multi-amp sense capture onto a driver-owned cyclic ring (SenseRing,
matching aop_spkr.rs):

- Arm the ADMAC RX ring on the stopped serializer immediately before
  every spkr pwrd transition so ring offset 0 is always slot 0 of a
  frame, and stop it after pw0 (releasing the ring and channel on spkr
  shutdown while the fabric is still powered).
- On a playback re-prepare while spkr is already running, mute the
  speaker codecs before cycling pw0 -> ring start -> pwrd (propagating
  any mute error to abort the clock transition so amps never see BCLK
  stop while active), and drop PAUSE/RESUME on playback so the playback
  DMA never resumes mid-frame either.
- Deliver whole-frame chunks in 2.5 ms (120-frame) periods from the
  80 ms ring to the attached VMALLOC sense front-end; signal XRUN before
  copying if the incoming frames would overrun unread capture data in
  the ALSA buffer, and re-check ring lap timing after the copy before
  publishing the updated front-end pointer.
- Keep the mono T8152 (sense_ring = false) path unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
